// Deep groove ball bearing 6800, 10 x 19 x 5 mm, shielded on both faces:
// the outer and inner steel rings and the shields between them. Its axis
// along z, a face at z = 0, centered on the origin.
// https://www.nsk.com/engineering/6800-apn.html
//
// From NSK's page for the 6800: 10 x 19 x 5 mm, dynamic load rating 1890 N,
// static 840 N, about 5 g. SKF sells the same size as the 61800, rated
// 1720 N and 830 N, 4.7 g: the sheet gives NSK's.
// The bore, outside diameter and width are ISO 15's for the designation,
// so any maker's 6800 has them. The rings' section and the shields are
// drawn, not measured. To hold it in a printed part, `bearing_seat.c2f`
// cuts its pocket.

// @description Deep groove ball bearing 6800, 10 mm bore, 19 mm outside, 5 mm
// @description wide: a thin-section bearing for a 10 mm shaft where there is
// @description little room around it.
// @spec bearing: deep groove ball bearing, single row, 6800 (NSK 6800)
// @spec bore: 10 mm
// @spec outside diameter: 19 mm
// @spec width: 5 mm
// @spec dynamic load: 1.89 kN
// @spec static load: 0.84 kN
// @spec mass: 5 g
// @source https://www.nsk.com/engineering/6800-apn.html NSK 6800 (dimensions, load ratings, mass)
// @source https://kramp.com/shop-de/en/p/deep-groove-ball-bearing-10x19x5mm-skf--61800SKF SKF 61800, the same size, at Kramp

use <lib/ball_bearing.c2f>

module bearing_6800() {
    ball_bearing(10, 19, 5);
}

bearing_6800();
